# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug/
target/

# Cargo.lock is intentionally NOT ignored: this is a binary crate, so the lock
# file must be committed for reproducible builds. Without it every build (and
# every CI run) resolves dependency versions afresh and can silently pick up a
# breaking patch release.
# See https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# Environment files. The bot token arrives via DISCORD_TOKEN, so this is the one
# file most likely to hold a live credential. `.env.example` stays tracked as the
# documented template; only real environment files are ignored.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/
# Vendored Discord API reference. This is a LOCAL, read-only copy and must not
# be committed: the upstream pages contain fake example credentials (OAuth2
# access/refresh tokens, client secrets) that a secret scanner cannot tell apart
# from real leaks. Keeping the copy out of git keeps the full-history secret scan
# meaningful, and the code comments still cite `docs/<page>.md` for the reader
# who has the reference next to the checkout.
docs/
